### Findings

- F1 [Major] Part 2, spec.md W4 group 6 and W7: the group 6 commit 3839d1d2 also changed
  `measure/tracks/math-app-retire-old-apps_20261114/spec-review.md` (an Author Note and an
  Accepted Risk line), a file outside the W4 group 6 list of `{spec,plan}.md` and outside
  the scope of this track. Rationale: W4 names the two files of group 6, and W7 keeps the
  review and audit reports out of scope; a change to an out-of-list file needed a spec
  change first. The commit note itself records that the change had no review.
- F2 [Nit] spec.md W1, `README.md:124`, `measure/architecture.md:140`,
  `measure/index.md:34`, `measure/product.md:46`: four planned markers hold two track ids
  each, against the W1 form `(planned: <track id>)`. Rationale: each track id stays on one
  line and `git grep` finds it, so the W1 purpose holds; a one-id form matches the given
  example of W1.
- F3 [Nit] plan.md first task, `evidence.md` lines 96 to 103: the plan names four sections
  of `evidence.md` (Facts, Unchanged Files, INTEGRATION Sections, Test Constraints), but
  the file also holds a "Phase 1 Checks" section. Rationale: the extra section records the
  pending checkpoint commands; it changes no deliverable.
- F4 [Nit] spec.md AC2: the phrase "in the group 3 files where it applies" leaves the
  choice of which group 3 document holds each marker to the implementer. Rationale: the
  mandatory half of AC2 (`README.md` or `AGENTS.md`) is decidable, and the committed
  documents satisfy it; the discretionary half is a small placement choice in a docs-only
  track.
